1
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and even my shoes fly off.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
Onto the head of the
carpenter I had in a chokehold,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
Katsushika Kameari,
another yawn, nothing changes.

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,220
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,440
the sunset falls into the great sky.

10
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow, too,
will end just like this, won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
even happiness lost again.

12
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:02,540
Coming now!

13
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:14,560
Ryo-sama

14
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:17,900
H-hey, don't just come in, Maria!

15
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:20,800
Ryo-sama, don't be so bashful.

16
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:23,360
We're husband and wife from today,
aren't we?

17
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:24,960
Was that so?

18
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:28,720
Ryo-sama, I'm so happy.

19
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:29,940
Th-that's, that's...

20
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:32,320
Me too, yes, just a moment!

21
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:34,920
Ryo-sama!

22
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,120
Stop it, stop it, stop it, stop it!

23
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:39,560
Stop it!

24
00:02:44,940 --> 00:02:46,100
Was that a good dream?

25
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,420
I had a crazy dream
first thing this morning.

26
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:04,860
Good morning, Ryo-sama.

27
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:10,040
Maria, what are you doing here?

28
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:14,380
Right, I'm still dreaming.

29
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:17,220
It has to be a dream, this dream.

30
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:20,060
Wake up, wake up, wake up already!

31
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:26,120
What are you going on about, Ryo-sama?
Are you still half asleep?

32
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:28,760
Why are you here?

33
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:32,680
I have nowhere else to go.

34
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:33,620
What do you mean?

35
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:37,780
I asked if I could live in the same dormitory as you,
Ryo-sama.

36
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:41,060
But they told me I can't stay like this.

37
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:42,320
Of course not!

38
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,380
Then why don't you go
live in the women's dorm?

39
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:48,460
They turned me down because I'm a man, too,

40
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:52,380
so I've decided to just
move into Master Ryo's room.

41
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:53,520
Don't decide things on your own!

42
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:55,620
Is it really not allowed?

43
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:01,140
Don't look at me with
those lovey-dovey eyes!

44
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:04,500
You're the only one at the police station I can rely on,
Master Ryo.

45
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:06,900
What am I supposed to do?

46
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:09,360
Don't cry.

47
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:12,800
Fine, fine, do whatever you want.

48
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:15,940
It can't be helped, can it?

49
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:18,380
Well, it's a win-win for both of us.

50
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:18,520
Stop it!

51
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:27,020
I've had this book out for ages,
I should give it back.

52
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:30,880
Senpai.

53
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,120
Senpai.

54
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,600
Hold me tight.

55
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,240
Did I get the wrong room?

56
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,900
No, it's Senpai's room after all.

57
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:44,840
Who's that?

58
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:48,800
It's Honda. Come in, come in.

59
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,820
G-good morning.

60
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:54,000
S-senpai, who is she?
That beautiful woman...

61
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:56,260
What? H-hey, get away from her!

62
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:59,920
She was just assigned to
Katsushika Police Station.

63
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:03,380
I'm Asato Ai. Please call me Maria.

64
00:05:03,740 --> 00:05:06,880
Nice to meet you,
I'm Honda from the later class.

65
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:07,598
Mr. Honda,

66
00:05:07,648 --> 00:05:11,340
would you like to join us for breakfast?
I'll get it ready right away.

67
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:13,040
Stay and eat, stay and eat.

68
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:15,140
Are you still eating?

69
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:28,480
A proper breakfast!
When was the last time you had one?

70
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:30,280
The salmon's almost done grilling.

71
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:34,320
What's wrong, Honda? Don't hold back.
Dig in, it's really good!

72
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:37,460
I always thought you'd stay single, senpai.

73
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:40,100
And with such a stunning beauty, too!

74
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:42,580
That's a misunderstanding. Listen?

75
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:45,900
A-a man?

76
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:46,620
Yeah.

77
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:49,140
Please stop with such an obvious lie.

78
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,380
Even from you, senpai, that's a harsh joke.

79
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:53,380
Lucky you, senpai.

80
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:56,800
I'm gonna get dumped
forever and end up single

81
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,400
Why does everything
always turn out like this?

82
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,840
So in the end,
all I've got is my motorcycle?

83
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:03,560
Lucky you, senpai.

84
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,540
Don't go sulking on your own.

85
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,640
I told you, Maria's a man!

86
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:07,880
Alright, bring it on!

87
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:10,860
Maria!

88
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:11,340
Yes?

89
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:12,340
One, two, three!

90
00:06:13,420 --> 00:06:15,720
Ha, bulge...

91
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:28,240
Damn! I forgot Maria was a
former kickboxing champion!

92
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:39,420
I'm really sorry, Honda-san.

93
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:41,900
No, it was my fault.

94
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:44,760
You're not to fight from now on.

95
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:49,100
Listen, you're a former
professional kickboxing champion.

96
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,480
So to speak, you're a walking lunatic.

97
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:53,360
Even to protect Ryo-sama?

98
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:56,000
Absolutely not! Understood?

99
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:58,960
Yes, I'll do exactly as Ryo-sama says.

100
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:01,920
You're not only cute, but obedient too.

101
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:05,860
But I can't believe such a beauty is a man.

102
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:07,940
Well, I feel the same way too.

103
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:11,120
I even considered marrying you at one point.

104
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:13,800
I'm always up for it, though.

105
00:07:15,580 --> 00:07:19,120
Even knowing it's just a flash,
this feel is nice, isn't it?

106
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:24,820
No, no, no! Two men can get married, but

107
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:29,140
I love you this much, and you still hate me?

108
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:33,760
It's not about liking or hating,
it's just that, you know, with a man...

109
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:39,300
Senpai, you have to understand Maria's feminine heart,
or she'll be so pitiful.

110
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,740
Where's the feminine heart?

111
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:43,120
It's a man's heart, because he's a man!

112
00:07:43,120 --> 00:07:47,000
Sometimes a man falls for a man's heart,
doesn't he?

113
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:48,620
That's not what I meant.

114
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:52,020
I adored you, Ryo-sama, so much that
I became disrespectful, and yet...

115
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:55,540
Oh no, I went and let him hold me.

116
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:56,780
Sorry about that.

117
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:59,540
I'll try to think of you as a woman.

118
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:02,260
I'll make an effort in my own way, somehow.

119
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,340
So don't cry.

120
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:07,200
Really, I'm so happy.

121
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:10,580
I can't tell if I feel
good or bad about this.

122
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,240
It doesn't make any sense.

123
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,620
Thanks for the meal.

124
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:21,180
Right, I'll go find a room for Maria.

125
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:25,820
If I think of you as a woman,
we can't possibly live together, can we?

126
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:28,820
Women aren't allowed in and
out of the men's dormitory.

127
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:30,820
But...

128
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:31,212
Relax,

129
00:08:31,262 --> 00:08:35,100
if I negotiate for you, even the
women's dormitory warden won't refuse.

130
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:36,540
Leave it to me.

131
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:39,500
Ryo-san really is dependable after all.

132
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:52,140
Did you really see it?

133
00:08:52,140 --> 00:08:53,080
It's true.

134
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:54,780
There's no mistake about that one.

135
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,180
It should be around here, though.

136
00:08:56,180 --> 00:08:56,820
Thanks, I'm counting on you.

137
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:59,220
She'll be moving in as
early as tomorrow, so.

138
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:00,580
That one's...

139
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,620
With me negotiating for her,
it'll be a piece of cake.

140
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:06,440
Let's hurry back and tell Maria.

141
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:11,060
No doubt about it.

142
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,280
It's Iwatetsu Heights.

143
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:14,040
I never expected her to
sneak into the police.

144
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:20,800
What is it? What do you want?

145
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,680
What, are you two here to
pitch newspaper subscriptions?

146
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,960
At last, I've found you.

147
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,540
We meet again after a hundred years,
Iwatetsu Iwao!

148
00:09:28,880 --> 00:09:30,000
Iwatetsu Iwao!

149
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,460
That name sounds familiar somehow.

150
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:33,160
Iwatetsu!

151
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:34,700
Where did you hide the old man?

152
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:35,840
The old man!

153
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:39,280
What are you talking about?
I haven't hidden anything.

154
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:42,040
So you're going to keep playing innocent

155
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:46,260
Then I have no choice.
I'll make you talk by force, Kōtetsu Iwao!

156
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,200
Aaaaaah!

157
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:50,820
Stop! You've got the wrong man!
I'm not Kōtetsu!

158
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,280
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu!

159
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:53,760
No questions!

160
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,360
It's Ryoko Mizuhiro-chan!

161
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:57,800
Where? Where?

162
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:59,340
Aaaaaah!

163
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,900
Waaaaaah!

164
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,020
Waaaah!

165
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:09,340
You filthy bastards!

166
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:12,860
A ten-thousand-yen bill... wait

167
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:14,360
Wait!

168
00:10:14,440 --> 00:10:18,060
Hahaha,
you fall for this every time, Gantetsu!

169
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,920
Knock it off already!

170
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:22,980
Gantetsu!

171
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:33,620
I keep telling you I'm not Gantetsu!

172
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:36,320
If that's how you want it,
I've got a plan too!

173
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:42,480
We're Miya-chan and
Myu-chan from Bababa Fee!

174
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:44,640
Fool, do you think I'll
fall for a trick like that?

175
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:45,980
Ryo-chaaan!

176
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:52,740
We who keep going on

177
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:55,320
are feeling great

178
00:10:55,810 --> 00:10:58,820
with Bababa's Miyabāto

179
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:00,200
Bārdasee!

180
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,840
Ready, set!

181
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,720
Scary Game!

182
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:19,020


183
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:19,460
Ryo-sama!

184
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:21,680
What happened? Your face!

185
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,660
It's nothing. Just a scratch.

186
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:25,240
Are you all right, Senpai?

187
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:26,660
What on earth happened?

188
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,480
Out of nowhere, that gang of six kenpo guys

189
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:33,100
attacked me, mistaking me for
some guy named Iwatetsu Iwao.

190
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:36,560
Iwatetsu Iwao... isn't he Maria-chan's...

191
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:39,480
Yes, he was my coach when I was a kickboxer.

192
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:42,160
Right, the one whose face looked just like yours,
Senpai...

193
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:45,820
Yes. The ones who attacked you were
most likely my father's disciples.

194
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:46,940
Disciples?

195
00:11:46,940 --> 00:11:49,640
My father is a martial
artist and runs a dojo.

196
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,420
They must have come looking for me.

197
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:55,400
Does your father know Maria became a woman?

198
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:56,700
No, he doesn't.

199
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:58,960
Your father is going to be shocked,
isn't he?

200
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:01,100
He might end up bedridden from the shock.

201
00:12:02,620 --> 00:12:03,680
Found you.

202
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:05,020
You're not getting away this time.

203
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:06,840
We've contacted the Chairman.

204
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,080
You punks.

205
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:09,380
Ryo-san, help me!

206
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:11,780
I don't want to go back to my father.

207
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:13,320
Don't worry.

208
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:15,820
These guys still haven't
realized who you are.

209
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,640
Even disguised as a cop,
you can't hide that face.

210
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:21,580
I already told you,
you've got the wrong man!

211
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,840
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu!

212
00:12:26,540 --> 00:12:27,060
He's here!

213
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:28,900
The Chairman has arrived!

214
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:37,020
How nostalgic, it's a three-wheeled auto!

215
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:38,440
It's my father's car.

216
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,720
I'm a martial artist.

217
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:50,100
Morning and night.

218
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:12,340
Ahahahahahaha!

219
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:15,940
Don't just pop out of nowhere like that.

220
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:17,880
What's the deal with
that three-wheeled truck?

221
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:21,880
That was just a one-off gag.

222
00:13:21,880 --> 00:13:23,560
You pulled such a pointless stunt.

223
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:26,460
What did you do with Gantetsu's son's love?

224
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:28,120
I'm not Gantetsu.

225
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:30,780
This gentleman isn't the Gantetsu coach,

226
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:32,720
he's Kankichi Ryotsu-sama.

227
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:42,780
Uh-oh.

228
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:43,860
This is going to get us found out.

229
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:46,960
Maybe.

230
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:50,740
Hey, Dad,
what time do you finish work today?

231
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:54,980
If you don't mind, there's a French
restaurant I go to regularly up at Daikanzan.

232
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,040
Why don't we have dinner together tonight?

233
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:57,820
No.

234
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:01,020
Wanna collect Puri Puri stickers together?

235
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,620
Could you also give me
your cell phone number?

236
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:06,500
He's hitting on his own son!

237
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:09,720
Isn't that normal?

238
00:14:10,740 --> 00:14:13,060
I feel like we've met somewhere before.

239
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:16,580
Weren't you working as a party girl
or something in Roppongi before?

240
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:20,220
Commander,
please don't switch into Roppongi mode.

241
00:14:20,220 --> 00:14:21,760
Take care of Gantetsu first.

242
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:23,880
Right, I forgot.

243
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:26,040
Hey, Gantetsu, where's your son?

244
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:28,060
I've told you, I'm not Gantetsu, right?

245
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:30,840
Your son? I just met him!

246
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,820
What?

247
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:41,080
Aaaaaah!

248
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:42,220
Aaaaaah!

249
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:45,600
So I've become a woman...

250
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,940
Father...

251
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:49,360
Aaaaaah!

252
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,720
Aaaaaah!

253
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,140
Aaaaaah!

254
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:02,420
Please, just forget about me.

255
00:15:02,420 --> 00:15:04,280
Father, what -

256
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:07,980
What? Don't say such selfish things!

257
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:14,660
It's you who must inherit the
Bookshelf Swordsmanship I created!

258
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,840
That's why I've had coaches
train you since you were little,

259
00:15:17,890 --> 00:15:19,860
making you master every martial art,

260
00:15:19,860 --> 00:15:22,704
karate, judo, wrestling,

261
00:15:22,754 --> 00:15:24,860
kickboxing,

262
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:29,440
